WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.029
The accepted schedule specifies valve
model

2
00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:05.944
A, while the installed plate shows model
B.

3
00:00:06.064 --> 00:00:08.901
Record the mismatch and its exact
location.

4
00:00:09.021 --> 00:00:11.433
Do not decide from the model number alone

5
00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:13.612
whether the difference is harmless.

6
00:00:13.732 --> 00:00:16.633
Assess relevant materials, connection,
cleaning

7
00:00:16.753 --> 00:00:20.337
and functional implications with the
responsible experts.

8
00:00:20.457 --> 00:00:22.996
Retain the original observation even

9
00:00:23.116 --> 00:00:25.569
if the supplier later replaces the valve.

10
00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:28.771
Correction may restore the specified
valve,

11
00:00:28.891 --> 00:00:33.307
or a proposed design change may require an
authorized assessment.

12
00:00:33.427 --> 00:00:35.427
These are not the same route.

13
00:00:35.547 --> 00:00:40.005
Do not revise the acceptance criterion
merely to match what arrived.

14
00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:43.709
Define what verification follows the
approved action

15
00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:47.065
and whether earlier checks or later tests
are affected.

16
00:00:47.185 --> 00:00:51.153
Keep the decision and supporting rationale
linked to the finding.

17
00:00:51.773 --> 00:00:55.485
A purchase order for the replacement is
not closure evidence.

18
00:00:55.605 --> 00:00:57.605
After the authorized action,

19
00:00:57.725 --> 00:01:00.349
obtain the specified installation evidence

20
00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:02.943
and assess any related implications.

21
00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.063
Retain the original failure

22
00:01:05.183 --> 00:01:07.889
and the subsequent result as separate
records.

23
00:01:08.009 --> 00:01:11.081
A clean second result should not erase the
history

24
00:01:11.201 --> 00:01:15.084
or imply that the first configuration had
always complied.

25
00:01:15.704 --> 00:01:20.077
Conditional progression is specific to the
next qualification activity

26
00:01:20.197 --> 00:01:23.483
and requires a documented no-significant-
impact

27
00:01:23.603 --> 00:01:26.269
assessment and responsible authorization.

28
00:01:26.389 --> 00:01:29.184
For example, an unresolved gasket issue

29
00:01:29.304 --> 00:01:32.099
may prevent wetted-system challenges even

30
00:01:32.219 --> 00:01:36.123
if a separately assessed dry control-
display check could proceed.

31
00:01:36.243 --> 00:01:38.717
This is an illustration, not permission.

32
00:01:38.837 --> 00:01:43.531
Do not use a high completion percentage as
a substitute for the assessment.
